-rust-proxmox-backup (4.2.7-1) trixie; urgency=medium
-
-  * docs: warn in the FAQ that `apt upgrade` can leave a partial upgrade, as
-    only `apt full-upgrade` can remove packages to satisfy dependencies. Also
-    fix a typo in the pcat1 file format description.
-
-  * openid auth: log the full error chain if getting the authorization URL
-    fails, to ease diagnosing connection problems.
-
-  * fix #7823: tape: do not announce a data-in transfer for SCSI commands
-    without a data phase, which targets such as SCST rejected with an
-    ILLEGAL REQUEST error.
-
-  * tape: configuration: also reject drive or changer device paths already
-    used by another entry of the same type on update. Enforce unique drive
-    numbers within each changer on creation and update. Existing duplicates
-    can block edits until they are resolved.
-
-  * tape: permissions:
-    - check '/tape/device/{drive}' for backup, restore and the drive list, as
-      grants on this documented path were previously ignored.
-    - require Datastore.Read on the datastore and Tape.Write on the media pool
-      and drive when creating or updating tape backup jobs. Scheduled jobs run
-      as root@pam, so job editors could otherwise get a datastore written to
-      tape without having read access to it.
-
-  * tape restore: validate the datastore name read from tape and require the
-    snapshot name to match the one selected for restore, so corrupt or crafted
-    media cannot place temporary files outside of the restore directory.
-
-  * s3: validate object keys against the datastore layout when refreshing the
-    contents from the bucket, instead of using them as file paths unchecked.
-    Directory marker objects returned by some providers are now skipped.
-
-  * client: pxar: harden restore and extraction against crafted archives that
-    could write or link files outside of the target directory. Symlinks are
-    no longer followed when entering existing directories or overwriting
-    files, also for symlinks already in the target, and hardlink targets must
-    resolve beneath the target directory without passing through symlinks.
-
-  * update proxmox-rest-server to 1.1.1:
-    - only abort a worker task if its whole UPID matches. Previously, users
-      allowed to stop their own tasks could stop others' tasks through a
-      crafted UPID.
-    - fix #6267: remove old task logs and archives again on busy systems.
-    - harden authentication: mask the credential check runtime in the delay
-      for failed logins, skip malformed cookie pairs and prefer a ticket over
-      an API token in the same request.
-    - accept quoted and unquoted Forwarded header addresses with optional
-      ports, use the last proxy element and reject unterminated quotes.
-    - honor zero deflate weights in Accept-Encoding, stop logging redirects
-      and unchanged responses as failures, and log client errors as warnings.
-    - run all API authentication and permission checks through one shared
-      code path.
-
-  * update proxmox-s3-client to 1.4.2: prevent the passive request limit from
-    overriding the active one, and name 'limit-active-requests' as the
-    replacement in the 'put-rate-limit' deprecation notice.
-
-  * update proxmox-network-api to 1.0.6:
-    - fix #7329: allow listing interfaces configured with the IPv6 'auto'
-      method.
-    - keep dhcp, auto and loopback methods on unrelated updates instead of
-      switching to manual, which could drop IPv6 settings.
-    - reject non-static methods while an address or gateway is set for the
-      same address family.
-
-  * update proxmox-rate-limiter to 1.0.1: prevent frequent refill updates from
-    stalling low-rate traffic, and fix opening the shared limiter on aarch64.
